  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Fixed\n\n- `morphirup setup --yes` and extension package installation work on macOS 15. Before, they failed with `extension.io_error: Cannot access '…/store/extensions/packages/sha256': native error 13.` macOS 15 refuses to rename a directory that is not writable, even when the directory stays in the same parent, and the installer sealed a package (mode 0555) before it published it with a rename. macOS 26 allows that rename, so the macos-latest jobs passed. The installer now seals the package's contents before publication and the package root after it, while it still holds the state lock. An installation of a package that is already in the store seals the root if a publication was interrupted before it did.\n- Build: the release and its dry run also run the osx-arm64 setup journey on macOS 15 (`build-morphirup`, `os: macos-15`), beside macos-latest (macOS 26). That leg uploads nothing: the new `morphirup-build.yml` input `upload` (default `true`) is `false` for it, and the macos-latest leg still produces the osx-arm64 assets. Pull requests do not run it.\n\n### Changed\n\n- `morphirup setup` sets up from the [finos/morphir releases](https://github.com/finos/morphir/releases), the official place for Morphir releases, from the next release, `0.5.0-alpha.2`, on. It downloads from `https://github.com/finos/morphir/releases/download/v<version>/`, with the same `v<version>` tag and the same three redirect hosts (`github.com`, `release-assets.githubusercontent.com`, `objects.githubusercontent.com`, at most three redirects), and keeps its `release-checksum` assurance. There is no fallback to the finos/morphir-dotnet releases: a bundle whose asset URLs name finos/morphir-dotnet is refused. A release generation records `https://github.com/finos/morphir` as its repository; the candidate's `sourceRepository` still names finos/morphir-dotnet, where the code is built from.\n- The composed local-toolchains family moves from `0.1.0-preview.4` to `0.1.0-preview.5` ([finos/morphir#1171](https://github.com/finos/morphir/pull/1171), merged as `00a48d4a`), which differs from preview.4 only in the release repository of the bundle's asset URLs and of the generation's `acquisition.repository`. The producer writes preview.5, and `morphirup` reads preview.5 only: candidates, bundles, receipts, selections and generations of preview.4 (written by 0.5.0-alpha.1) are not read and are not converted. `select`, `show` and `run` read only the preview.5 selection pointer: in a Home set up with preview.2, preview.3 or preview.4 they refuse with `local.setup_required`, which says to run `morphirup setup --yes` again (and then `select`, for a local candidate). Setup in that Home installs preview.5 beside the earlier generations without reading them, and replaces the selection pointer. A refused `setup`, `select` or `show` writes a preview.5 result. The historical preview.1 local route is unchanged.\n- Build: finos/morphir can call `morphirup-build.yml` at a pinned commit of this repository, as it calls `cli-offering.yml`. The new inputs `repository` and `ref` (a full commit SHA) choose what the job checks out and builds, and the Windows source check compares the checkout with `ref`. With the new input `upload-host-offering: true`, a job that packs a toolchain (win-x64, win-arm64, or osx-arm64 with `toolchain: true`) also uploads its self-contained host as the artifact `morphir-dotnet-self-contained-<rid>`: the archive with its `.build-launch.json`, `.build-contents.json` and `.sha256`, the files `cli-offering.yml` uploads for that offering. The inputs default to empty and `false`, so `morphirup.yml` and `deployment.yml` work as before. The checkout no longer keeps the workflow token in the Git configuration.",
